# Citations

myMedKitt cites authoritative sources (AHA/ASA, ACEP, ACOG, EMCrit/IBCC, specialty
guidelines) so a clinician can independently verify the basis for any recommendation —
this is also what preserves the app's CDS posture.

Citations in this skill are **per-consult**: each consult reference under
`references/consults/<id>.md` ends with its own numbered `Citations` section, generated
verbatim from that consult's source-of-truth citations array. There is no single global
bibliography because the skill spans {{consult_count}} consults; the relevant references
travel with each consult.

When a guideline updates, the fix is made in the app's source and the skill is rebuilt —
never hand-edit a citation here.
